{
    "_comment": [
        "Path -> Playwright spec map for affected-only E2E selection on ready-PR incremental pushes.",
        "Consumed by tools/playwright_spec_selection.py; wired into .github/workflows/ci-e2e-playwright.yml.",
        "The selector is FAIL-CLOSED: any changed file not matched below forces the FULL suite, and a",
        "selection miss is caught by the post-merge full run on master (the backstop). Start narrow and",
        "widen `scenes`/`explicit` as recall data comes in. Every target must resolve to >=1 real spec",
        "(enforced by tools/test_playwright_spec_selection.py) and point only into the two spec roots.",
        "Glob syntax: `*` matches within a path segment, `**` matches across segments (only at pattern end).",
        "A target ending in `/` is a directory prefix (all specs beneath it); otherwise it's an exact file.",
        "Every spec must be reachable by some target OR listed in `full_suite_only` — the test enforces",
        "this, so adding a spec forces a conscious choice: map it, or accept it only runs in full suites",
        "(and when directly edited).",
        "`ignore` lists paths that provably CANNOT affect the app under test (docs, agent instructions,",
        "lint rules, workflows for other suites): they contribute nothing to selection instead of forcing",
        "a full run. `force_full` outranks `ignore`, no ignore pattern may match a spec (test-enforced),",
        "and an all-ignored diff still runs the full suite (category `all_ignored`) until telemetry",
        "justifies a skip mode. Only add entries that cannot reach the app bundle, the backend, or the",
        "e2e stack config.",
        "`scenes_smoke_only` lists scenes with NO direct e2e coverage — no spec navigates to them, so",
        "the full suite wouldn't exercise them either. Changes there run `smoke_subset` (app boots,",
        "auth works) instead of everything. A scene must not appear in both `scenes` and",
        "`scenes_smoke_only` (test-enforced); when a scene gains a real spec, move it to `scenes`.",
        "`backend_smoke` lists backend Python paths (and their pytest snapshots) that run",
        "`backend_smoke_specs` instead of everything when no earlier rule maps them; a file that also",
        "falls in a `backend_explicit` area adds that area's specs. The merge queue and master pushes",
        "still run the full suite, so a backend regression outside those specs first fails there.",
        "`force_full` and `explicit` both outrank it, so keep high-blast-radius backend paths",
        "(migrations, settings, URL routing, auth, middleware, the e2e setup endpoint, demo data,",
        "backend for `full_suite_only` specs) in `force_full`. `backend_explicit` only applies to files",
        "`backend_smoke` matched, so non-Python files under the backend trees stay unmapped and force a",
        "full run. `backend_smoke_specs` must include a spec whose workspace seeds demo data",
        "(dashboards does): `auth` skips demo data, so it alone misses a broken workspace setup."
    ],
